1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
I had an interview today, too.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:03,829
I had a great interview

3
00:00:03,829 --> 00:00:05,956
with Admissions at Columbia University.

4
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:06,346
Really?

5
00:00:06,346 --> 00:00:07,906
What did they say?

6
00:00:07,906 --> 00:00:10,374
Will you get into the school?

7
00:00:10,374 --> 00:00:11,912
Well, they didn't say anything for sure.

8
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:15,390
But I figure that with my grades and with my personality,

9
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:18,308
I'll have no problem.

10
00:00:18,308 --> 00:00:20,068
Columbia's a terrific school.

11
00:00:20,068 --> 00:00:21,346
What are you going to do?

12
00:00:21,346 --> 00:00:24,224
Do? I don't know.

13
00:00:24,224 --> 00:00:27,231
I also applied to NYU.

14
00:00:27,231 --> 00:00:29,373
You sound excited about Columbia.

15
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:31,970
What's your problem, Mike?

16
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:32,989
Indecision. Indecision.

17
00:00:32,989 --> 00:00:33,681
It's not easy,

18
00:00:33,681 --> 00:00:36,283
and this is an important decision we have to make.

19
00:00:36,283 --> 00:00:37,923
What about you?

20
00:00:37,923 --> 00:00:39,214
How was your interview with Michigan?

21
00:00:39,214 --> 00:00:40,964
The interview was fine.

22
00:00:40,964 --> 00:00:42,292
It's a great college.

23
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:43,492
It is.

24
00:00:43,492 --> 00:00:46,075
My father would like me to go there.

25
00:00:46,075 --> 00:00:47,440
He and my Grandpa both went there.

26
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,147
Great medical school, too.

27
00:00:49,147 --> 00:00:52,465
I know.

28
00:00:52,465 --> 00:00:53,603
You can follow in your father's footsteps.

29
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:59,221
Ah! I'd like to follow in my own footsteps, Mike.

30
00:00:59,221 --> 00:01:00,892
What do you want to study?

31
00:01:00,892 --> 00:01:03,137
I've been thinking.

32
00:01:03,137 --> 00:01:05,515
I think I want to study journalism

33
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:07,035
to be a reporter--a newspaperman.

34
00:01:07,035 --> 00:01:11,198
You do a pretty good job on the Riverdale High School paper.

35
00:01:11,198 --> 00:01:12,751
And I've been thinking about it a lot lately.

36
00:01:12,751 --> 00:01:14,449
Have you discussed it with your parents?

37
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,427
No. But I have to.

38
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:22,905
OK. Let's talk.

39
00:01:22,905 --> 00:01:34,317
Hi, Son. Is everything all right?

40
00:01:34,317 --> 00:01:37,295
Hi, Dad. Everything's fine.

41
00:01:37,295 --> 00:01:39,384
I was just waiting for you to get home

42
00:01:39,384 --> 00:01:40,273
so we could talk.

43
00:01:40,273 --> 00:01:43,251
Anything special you want to talk about?

44
00:01:43,251 --> 00:01:44,229
There is, Dad.

45
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,207
I'm listening.

46
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:52,493
Well, I know you and Mom have given up a lot

47
00:01:52,493 --> 00:01:54,239
to save money for my college tuition.

48
00:01:54,239 --> 00:01:56,640
We want you to go to college, Robbie.

49
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:01,118
I know. I do.

50
00:02:01,118 --> 00:02:02,096
But?

51
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:05,447
Well, I've thought a lot about which college,

52
00:02:05,447 --> 00:02:09,719
and one of them is Columbia.

53
00:02:09,719 --> 00:02:12,030
Columbia? Why Columbia?

54
00:02:12,030 --> 00:02:17,653
First, they have an excellent School of Journalism.

55
00:02:17,653 --> 00:02:19,964
They do.

56
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:24,582
And your friends are planning to go to Columbia?

57
00:02:24,582 --> 00:02:25,920
That's only part of it.

58
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:28,898
It's complicated.

59
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,876
I'll try to explain.

60
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:36,187
Mike and I had a hamburger this afternoon, and we talked.

61
00:02:36,187 --> 00:02:37,832
Yes?

62
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:40,810
Well, we talked about a lot of things.

63
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:42,134
He applied to Columbia,

64
00:02:42,134 --> 00:02:44,061
and his interview was very successful.

65
00:02:44,061 --> 00:02:45,424
He thinks he'll be accepted,

66
00:02:45,424 --> 00:02:48,266
and he really wants to go there.

67
00:02:48,266 --> 00:02:52,112
Dean Rafer called me today.

68
00:02:52,112 --> 00:02:55,700
He told me he was very impressed with you.

69
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,700
He's a nice man.

70
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:58,678
He was very kind.

71
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,656
He told me

72
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:04,634
you had some doubts about wanting to go to Michigan.

73
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:07,612
Yes. I do.

74
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:10,589
I'm just not sure about what I want to do.

75
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:13,567
That's OK.

76
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:16,545
You understand?

77
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:19,523
Let me tell you something, Robbie.

78
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:27,399
Something that might be surprising to you.

79
00:03:27,399 --> 00:03:31,435
What? Tell me.

80
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:37,391
Well, Grandpa wanted me to study engineering, like him.

81
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:41,809
Well, I wasn't clear about my future,

82
00:03:41,809 --> 00:03:48,325
but I knew engineering was not for me.

83
00:03:48,325 --> 00:03:52,281
What did you tell Grandpa?

84
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:55,259
The truth.

85
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:56,739
Then you're not upset

86
00:03:56,739 --> 00:04:01,215
about my not wanting to go into medicine?

87
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:03,215
I'm not upset at all.

88
00:04:03,215 --> 00:04:07,171
I'm just happy that we're able to talk about it.

89
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:10,149
I am too, Dad.

90
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:15,127
I suppose you want to apply to Columbia.

91
00:04:15,127 --> 00:04:21,083
Yes, but I also want to apply to several other colleges.

92
00:04:21,083 --> 00:04:22,901
I thought you wanted to go to Columbia.

93
00:04:22,901 --> 00:04:25,038
Well, I might want to go to Columbia.

94
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:28,016
But I might not.

95
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:30,994
I just want to be able to make my own decision.

96
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:33,972
You're a real Stewart!

97
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:39,928
And if I think about it long enough, you never know ...

98
00:04:39,928 --> 00:04:40,928
Never know what?

99
00:04:40,928 --> 00:04:42,906
If I make my own decision,

100
00:04:42,906 --> 00:04:48,862
I might choose Michigan.

101
00:04:48,862 --> 00:04:51,840
Robbie, you're something!

102
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:54,818
You know, when I was your age,

103
00:04:54,818 --> 00:04:57,818
I said exactly the same thing to Grandpa.
